{
  "version": "2.17",
  "children": [
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "JnygO",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Brief · Activos",
      "width": 360,
      "fill": "$bg-muted",
      "cornerRadius": "$radius-md",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": "$space-4",
      "padding": "$space-5",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "WpnvG",
          "name": "BT",
          "fill": "$fg-default",
          "content": "Activos — brief",
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 18,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "B73zD0",
          "name": "BB",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "kit-version-source: 1.0.0 · updated: 2026-09-16\n\n1. PURPOSE\nThe Activos tab: the three tiers of interest in a symbol (D9, named per D48) — Holdings (open positions), Watchlist (watchlist_items) and Tracked (the catalogue the instance syncs) — plus the two ways data gets in: the trade sheet and the CSV importer. Historial holds the three lists with no other home (D43, D60).\n\n2. ENTRY POINTS\n- Holdings / Watchlist — BottomNav tab (/assets, assets#index; ?tab=watchlist)\n- Registrar movimiento — the primary button above the tabs opens /trades/new inside a <dialog> (D11, components/_sheet_dialog); the asset detail opens it pre-filled\n- Historial, Importar movimientos, Tracked — the three foot-of-list rows under either tab (/positions, /trades/import, /tracked). All three carry HeaderBar back to /assets\n- Rows link to the asset detail in cockpit.pen\n\n3. SCREENS (left → right)\n- Holdings · Default — summary, the sheet button, holdings by market value (D68)\n- Watchlist · Default — rows ordered by distance to their own alert threshold, then by day move (D68)\n- Holdings · Vacío — nothing open: no summary, the empty state's door is the importer\n- Watchlist · Vacía\n- Holdings · Sin consolidar — no FX rate: the notice replaces the summary\n- Registrar movimiento · Sheet — a USD buy into a held position: projection and FX card showing\n- Registrar movimiento · Con teclado — D11's acceptance: the footer survives the keyboard (the note beside it)\n- Registrar movimiento · CETES — a fixed-income buy asks for Vencimiento; MXN hides the FX card\n- Historial · Default — Movimientos, Dividendos cobrados, Posiciones cerradas\n- Historial · Vacío\n- Tracked · Default — catalogue rows, the budget last on mobile\n- Tracked · Agregar activo — the typeahead and the six fields it fills (D64)\n- Tracked · Sin fuente — an asset the provider cannot name, with its fix in place (D46)\n- Tracked · Sin coincidencias — a filter that matches nothing\n- Importar CSV · Default, Revisión, Símbolos desconocidos (#401, D62, D63, D65)\n- Desktop band: Holdings, Registrar movimiento (the same dialog, centred) and Tracked (list beside the budget). The rest reflow (D4)\n\n4. BUSINESS RULES\n- The summary renders only while something is open; without an FX rate it becomes the Sin consolidar notice and rows keep their own currency, alphabetical (trading/use_cases/load_assets.rb)\n- Money per D10: the summary declares the currency, rows in it drop the symbol, anything else keeps its ISO prefix. Historial's trade and dividend rows keep theirs because they mix\n- A holding row leads with its value and follows with the day's move, a dash when there is no previous close (D69, ADR-021). No state chip, no confluence dots (D85)\n- A watchlist row reads \"falta X%\" when an alert threshold exists, \"sigues ±X%\" from entry_price otherwise\n- The sheet asks for Vencimiento only on a fixed-income buy; the FX card hides when the currency is blank or MXN; the average-cost projection shows only on a buy into the held symbol in its own currency (trades/new.html.erb, trade_sheet_controller.js)\n- Tracked counts the whole catalogue; the filter narrows the list only. Seguir shows on the Tracked tier alone; a paused row dims, a sourceless one does not (D46)\n- The budget bar is in spend order — Holdings, Watchlist, the rest — over active stocks and ETFs only (D82)\n- An import is all-or-nothing unless the owner chooses to leave the unknown symbols out\n\n5. COPY SOURCE\nconfig/locales/es-MX.yml — assets.index, assets.tracked, trades.new, positions.index, trade_imports.*, comun.sin_tc_*. Row figures: AssetsHelper. FX note date: FxRatesController (date_label).\n\n6. STATES NOT DRAWN\n- \"Guardado. Registra el siguiente.\" above the sheet after Guardar y registrar otro\n- The importer's error line, and the other refusals (invalid_rows, missing_fx_history, repeated_external_ids, unsupported_asset_type): the same card with the detail listed below it\n- Tracked with an empty catalogue — the empty state reads \"Tu instancia aún no rastrea ningún activo.\"\n- The budget exhausted or unlimited — \"Agotado hasta mañana\" / \"Sin límite\"\n- Inline edit and delete of a movement in Historial — MovementItem has no action slot in the kit\n- The typeahead results are an overlay in code; the artboard draws them in flow\n- A Watchlist tab with nothing held — the summary is absent\n- Empty states and the drop zone have a dashed border — the .pen format has none\n\n7. OPEN FINDINGS\nNone.\n\n8. HISTORY\n→ Log frame, below this brief. Reasoning before 2026-09-16: git show 120600bb:design/V2_REMAINING.md (ACT-*).",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
